        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Māori King movement</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a>'s North Island: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waikato">Waikato</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-country">King Country</a> of the Ngāti Maniapoto, and Taranaki; its headquarters is <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turangawaewae">Tūrangawaewae</a> Marae at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ngaruawahia">Ngāruawāhia</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">Rūnanga revived around 1853; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potatau-te-wherowhero">Pōtatau Te Wherowhero</a> crowned in 1858; the invasion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waikato">Waikato</a> from 1863 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tawhiao">Tāwhiao</a>'s exile of about 20 years; the Kauhanganui from 1892; the monarchs from Mahuta (1894) to Nga wai hono i te po (2024).</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Leading figures</span><span class="info-stat-val">Tāmihana Te Rauparaha, who first proposed a Māori kingdom; Wiremu Tamihana, the kingmaker; the kings <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potatau-te-wherowhero">Pōtatau Te Wherowhero</a>, Matutaera <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tawhiao">Tāwhiao</a>, Mahuta, Te Rata and Korokī; Queen Te Atairangikaahu; King Tūheitia; Queen Nga wai hono i te po; Te Puea Hērangi, chief organiser.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">Defeat at Ōrākau in 1864 and the confiscation of 486,500 hectares of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waikato">Waikato</a> land; a movement that endures as a non-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitutional-monarchy">constitutional monarchy</a> outside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> government, headed today by Nga wai hono i te po.</span></div>
